{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00432",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.4,
      "end_seconds": 6.87,
      "duration_seconds": 5.47,
      "text": "Hi, doctor, I brought my bag, is it fine to leave it here?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.45,
      "end_seconds": 10.75,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "Right on time. Sit, please. How can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 11.15,
      "end_seconds": 15.33,
      "duration_seconds": 4.18,
      "text": "Hello, doctor, I came in with them, if that's okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 18.77,
      "end_seconds": 21.89,
      "duration_seconds": 3.12,
      "text": "Good, that'll be useful. Pull up a chair."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 22.49,
      "end_seconds": 34.27,
      "duration_seconds": 11.78,
      "text": "Um, so... breathlessness on the stairs. That's why I came. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest. I did try to ignore it for a while."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 35.25,
      "end_seconds": 40.41,
      "duration_seconds": 5.16,
      "text": "When did you first notice it? These questions might sound routine, but they matter."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 41.7,
      "end_seconds": 45.12,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "Hmm, it's been like this since last Tuesday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 46.24,
      "end_seconds": 48.03,
      "duration_seconds": 1.79,
      "text": "How often does it happen?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 48.91,
      "end_seconds": 50.81,
      "duration_seconds": 1.9,
      "text": "Honestly, every other day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 51.78,
      "end_seconds": 54.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "What makes it worse, if anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 54.51,
      "end_seconds": 57.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.1,
      "text": "Yes, climbing stairs. That makes it worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 58.47,
      "end_seconds": 60.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "How much is it bothering you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 61.72,
      "end_seconds": 67.96,
      "duration_seconds": 6.24,
      "text": "I'd say mild. Yeah, I was feeling tired at one point, but that's gone now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 71.26,
      "end_seconds": 73.18,
      "duration_seconds": 1.92,
      "text": "Any chest pain or black stools?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 73.71,
      "end_seconds": 75.35,
      "duration_seconds": 1.64,
      "text": "Nothing like that, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 75.77,
      "end_seconds": 79.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.36,
      "text": "Have you had any fainting, heavy periods or weight loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 79.63,
      "end_seconds": 84.09,
      "duration_seconds": 4.46,
      "text": "I haven't had fainting, heavy periods or weight loss, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 84.66,
      "end_seconds": 96.99,
      "duration_seconds": 12.33,
      "text": "Just so you know how the rest of the visit will go: I'll finish my notes, we'll agree on the plan, and the front desk will help with anything that needs booking. You shouldn't need to chase anything yourself."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 98.29,
      "end_seconds": 101.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.07,
      "text": "Good, I was wondering how this would go."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.27,
      "end_seconds": 108.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "Do you have any allergies to medicines, food, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 108.9,
      "end_seconds": 111.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "No, nothing I'm aware of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 112.2,
      "end_seconds": 116.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.87,
      "text": "So, moving on to your background, any past medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 117.42,
      "end_seconds": 130.43,
      "duration_seconds": 13.01,
      "text": "I've got acid reflux. I'm hoping you can tell me something definite. Yes, heart disease. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing. I thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 131.18,
      "end_seconds": 132.13,
      "duration_seconds": 0.95,
      "text": "Okay. Anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 133.61,
      "end_seconds": 145.39,
      "duration_seconds": 11.78,
      "text": "Right, so that's your known acid reflux. We'll keep that in mind today. Right, so that's your known heart disease. We'll keep that in mind today. What medicines are you taking at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 148.62,
      "end_seconds": 151.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "It's omeprazole, once a day, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 152.6,
      "end_seconds": 154.42,
      "duration_seconds": 1.82,
      "text": "How much do you take?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 155.49,
      "end_seconds": 162.43,
      "duration_seconds": 6.94,
      "text": "20 milligrams. He is on aspirin, 75 milligrams, once a day for my heart, I give it to him."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 162.65,
      "end_seconds": 163.37,
      "duration_seconds": 0.72,
      "text": "I see."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 164.44,
      "end_seconds": 168.55,
      "duration_seconds": 4.11,
      "text": "Give me a second, I'm just scrolling back through your chart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 169.04,
      "end_seconds": 169.78,
      "duration_seconds": 0.74,
      "text": "Of course."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 184.26,
      "end_seconds": 188.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting. What about operations, anything like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 189.57,
      "end_seconds": 193.58,
      "duration_seconds": 4.01,
      "text": "Just my thyroid operated on, a long time ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 194.47,
      "end_seconds": 197.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "Let's get your blood pressure and the other basics."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 210.24,
      "end_seconds": 212.16,
      "duration_seconds": 1.92,
      "text": "Okay, give me a moment..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 227.47,
      "end_seconds": 236.53,
      "duration_seconds": 9.06,
      "text": "Okay: temperature is 37.0 degrees, SpO2 97 percent on room air. And pulse is 106 beats a minute, blood pressure 121 over 83."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.38,
      "end_seconds": 241.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "Okay, let's do a quick examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 242.87,
      "end_seconds": 243.82,
      "duration_seconds": 0.95,
      "text": "Yes, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 245.65,
      "end_seconds": 248.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "A little pressure here, tell me if it's tender."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.6,
      "end_seconds": 265.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "Heart sounds are normal, I don't hear any murmur."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 266.42,
      "end_seconds": 267.12,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.02,
      "end_seconds": 271.63,
      "duration_seconds": 2.61,
      "text": "Tell me if anything hurts as I press."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 281.94,
      "end_seconds": 283.63,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "Your eyelids are pale inside."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 285.76,
      "end_seconds": 308.06,
      "duration_seconds": 22.3,
      "text": "All done, thank you, please sit down. Thank you for that. I'll write up what I found in a moment, and then I'll tell you what I think is going on. So, based on the history and the examination, my working impression is anaemia of some kind. That's my thinking for now, and it may change as we learn more."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 309.6,
      "end_seconds": 312.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.53,
      "text": "Should I be worried about this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 313.38,
      "end_seconds": 330.33,
      "duration_seconds": 16.95,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now anaemia of some kind is my leading thought, not anything worse. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had breathlessness on the stairs, since last Tuesday, mild, and no fainting or black stools."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 331.03,
      "end_seconds": 332.93,
      "duration_seconds": 1.9,
      "text": "Yes, you've got it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 335.73,
      "end_seconds": 361.53,
      "duration_seconds": 25.8,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange a vitamin B12 level for possible deficiency. Let's get a ferritin level, for possible iron deficiency. I'd rather check than guess, and this is the quickest way to know more. Let's use ferrous sulfate, 200 milligrams, once a day, for three months. You take it by mouth. That should help with possible iron deficiency. Iron can darken the stools and bother the stomach, so take it after food."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 362.07,
      "end_seconds": 382.45,
      "duration_seconds": 20.38,
      "text": "Try to get to bed and wake up at the same time each day, and keep your phone away from the bed. Try to keep a simple diary of when it happens and what you were doing, and bring it to the next visit. I want you to come back or go to emergency straight away if the symptoms get worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 383.02,
      "end_seconds": 384.73,
      "duration_seconds": 1.71,
      "text": "Got it, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 386.03,
      "end_seconds": 388.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "I'd like to see you again in two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 392.24,
      "end_seconds": 393.8,
      "duration_seconds": 1.56,
      "text": "Okay, I'll book that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 395.4,
      "end_seconds": 398.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.61,
      "text": "Okay, I think we're finished. Is everything clear?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 399.54,
      "end_seconds": 404.15,
      "duration_seconds": 4.61,
      "text": "Okay, thank you. I'll get started on all of that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 405.41,
      "end_seconds": 407.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "Alright, bye for now, look after yourself."
    }
  ]
}